  "name": "Phase 3 — Mindoro Strait pilot",
  "description": "TTX pilot scenario in the Philippine Area of Responsibility: the whole planning layer in one exercise, in the Mindoro Strait between Mindoro and the Calamian Islands. Blue holds the strait with a sense zone and a polygon engage zone; a surface action group covers the Sulu Sea side and a corvette holds the passage as the zone's assigned shooter. Blue commands from the destroyer over a line-of-sight net relayed by the corvette, with the maritime HQ ashore at San Jose as the alternate (5-minute handover, orders queued). Red, a fictional opposing force, sends two corvettes south through the strait, one carrying a jammer, while a landing ship lays mines on the northern approach and a patrol boat runs a barrier patrol behind them. Blue has a mine countermeasures vessel sweeping that approach, an oiler on the Sulu Sea side, a patrol vessel low on fuel on a denial patrol, and a supply ship carrying stores from Coron that then stages at the Busuanga anchorage. Fuel is on. Dusk falls about 85 minutes in; a tropical-depression bulletin raises the sea state to 5 from 02:40 to 03:20. No real-world navy or state is represented: all platforms are generic database classes with no real-world values.",
